<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Repo-local SHADOW of PX4's Tools/simulation/gz/models/x500_base (ADR-0005
  resource-path-shadow mechanism -- resolves ahead of PX4's copy because
  launch scripts put $REPO_ROOT/models first in GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH).
  PX4's tree is untouched (ADR-0001).

  PURPOSE: portfolio demo video reskin ONLY. x500_base is the interceptor's
  visible body (gz_x500_mono_cam = x500 = x500_base + mono_cam), and the
  stock livery (light carbon-fiber weave, yellow antenna markers, blue FMU
  trim) reads too close to the enemy fpv_target model's dark carbon body.
  This shadow changes ONLY <material> blocks on 9 of the model's existing
  <visual> elements (below, 3 groups: 1 body + 4 motor-base + 4 motor-bell)
  to a dark-carbon-black body + electric-blue arm-tip accent -- clearly
  distinct from fpv_target's black+RED enemy scheme (blue=friendly /
  red=hostile, standard force-tracking convention).

  NOT CHANGED (verified byte-identical to PX4's original -- diff the two
  files with the 9 new <material> blocks below removed and there is no
  other delta): every <collision>, <inertial>, <link>/<joint> name, sensor
  definition, and all <mesh><uri>/<scale>/<pose> geometry references. Mesh
  and texture ASSETS themselves are not copied -- they're symlinked from
  PX4's tree (see meshes/ and materials/textures/) since GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH
  model:// resolution locks onto the FIRST resource-path root containing a
  model dir named "x500_base" and does not fall through per-file to other
  roots, so a shadow with a changed model.sdf but no local mesh files would
  fail to load (same self-containment requirement as the mono_cam FOV
  shadow noted in ADR-0011).

  Reskinned visuals (search "FPV RESKIN" below for each):
    - base_link_visual (main frame/arms/top-plate/landing-gear mesh,
      NXP-HGD-CF.dae) -> dark carbon black. This mesh bakes 9 separate
      COLLADA materials (CarbonFiber weave texture, Metal, 3x landing-gear
      plastics, FMUK66 case, yellow RailsAntennaHolder, blue FMURubber); an
      SDF <material> on a mesh visual overrides ALL of a mesh's embedded
      materials with one flat material (classic Gazebo/Ogre behavior,
      confirmed by PX4's own precedent two visuals down -- the prop STL
      visuals already rely on exactly this override), so there was no way
      to keep the multi-tone factory look while recoloring in place; the
      whole visual goes to one flat dark material.
    - 5010_motor_base_0..3 (the 4 visible motor-mount "cans" at each arm
      tip, 5010Base.dae, already separate <visual> elements in PX4's own
      SDF) -> electric blue with a touch of emissive. Using pre-existing
      separate visuals for the accent avoids adding any new geometry: the
      "colored arm accent" look comes from recoloring an existing element,
      not from a new primitive.
    - rotor_0..3's motor-bell visuals (5010Bell.dae, inconsistently named
      "..._visual_motor_bell" for rotor_0 and "..._visual_motor_top" for
      rotor_1..3 in PX4's own file -- not touched here) -> same dark carbon
      black as the body, for a cohesive blacked-out frame.
  Left stock (too small to matter / already dark / lowest risk):
    NXP_FMUK66_FRONT/TOP, RDDRONE_FMUK66_TOP (tiny 1.3x0.7cm FC-board
    decals) and the 4 prop STL visuals (already Gazebo/DarkGrey).

  CONFIDENCE NOTE for whoever verifies this: the "SDF <material> overrides
  a mesh's baked materials" claim is well-established classic-Gazebo/Ogre
  behavior and is already exercised by PX4's own prop-visual material
  script in this same file, but it was not re-confirmed by an actual gz
  render in this task (one-sim-at-a-time rule was in effect). Worst case if
  wrong: the body renders in its stock PX4 colors -- a purely cosmetic
  no-op, not a functional break (no collision/inertial/mesh-geometry/sensor
  touched). Boot gz_x500_mono_cam and look at it to confirm.
-->
<sdf version='1.9'>
  <model name='x500_base'>
    <pose>0 0 .24 0 0 0</pose>
    <self_collide>false</self_collide>
    <static>false</static>
    <link name="base_link">
      <inertial>
        <mass>2.0</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.02166666666666667</ixx>
          <ixy>0</ixy>
          <ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.02166666666666667</iyy>
          <iyz>0</iyz>
          <izz>0.04000000000000001</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
      <gravity>true</gravity>
      <velocity_decay />
      <visual name="base_link_visual">
        <pose>0 0 .025 0 0 3.141592654</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://x500_base/meshes/NXP-HGD-CF.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <!-- FPV RESKIN (visual-only, ADR interceptor-reskin): flat SDF material
             overrides ALL of NXP-HGD-CF.dae's baked submeshes (CarbonFiber,
             Metal, LandingFoam/Rubber/Plastic, FMUK66, RailsAntennaHolder,
             FMURubber) with one dark carbon-black finish. Geometry/mesh URI
             above is untouched. -->
        <material>
          <ambient>0.018 0.018 0.022 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.032 0.032 0.04 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.18 0.19 0.22 1</specular>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name="5010_motor_base_0">
        <pose>0.174 0.174 .032 0 0 -.45</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>1 1 1</scale>
            <uri>model://x500_base/meshes/5010Base.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <!-- FPV RESKIN: arm-tip accent color (electric blue, slight emissive
             pop for camera/demo footage), same override rationale as
             base_link_visual above. -->
        <material>
          <ambient>0.02 0.06 0.22 1</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.05 0.22 0.95 1</diffuse>
          <specular>0.3 0.45 0.95 1</specular>
          <emissive>0.02 0.08 0.35 1</emissive>
        </material>
      </visual>
